  "result": "`Cart.remove` now removes the Widget line, and all 7 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines on `l.item.name != sku`, so it compared the SKU you passed in with the item's display name. `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so nothing was ever removed.\n\n**Fix:** it now filters on `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `test_remove_by_sku` to `tests/test_pricing.py`. It recreates the demo cart and checks that only `sku-2` is left after the remove. I also ran `python3 -m shop.demo`: it now prints `1` where it used to print `2`.",
